<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2>Things patients often ask.</h2>
      <p>Don't see your question? Call us — we're happy to talk things through before you book.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">How often should I have a dental check-up? <span class="icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Twice a year is the right cadence for most people. If you have specific concerns — orthodontic treatment, gum sensitivity, recent dental work — we may suggest a slightly tighter rhythm. We'll build a plan that fits you.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Are root canals actually painful? <span class="icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Not anymore. Modern anaesthesia and gentler technique mean most patients describe the procedure as no worse than a routine filling. The point of a root canal is to remove pain, not cause it.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">How long do dental implants take? <span class="icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>The implant procedure itself is one appointment. Full healing (osseointegration with the bone) takes three to six months, after which we fit the permanent crown. We'll walk you through the full timeline at your consultation.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">Do you accept insurance? <span class="icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>We work with most major insurance providers. Call us at {{ site.phone_display }} or send a quick email and we'll check your coverage before you book.</p></div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item reveal">
        <div class="faq-q">What if I have a dental emergency? <span class="icon">+</span></div>
        <div class="faq-a"><p>Call us at {{ site.phone_display }} as soon as you can. We keep emergency slots open most days and will do our best to see you the same day.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

